WEBVTT

00:14:58.517 --> 00:15:00.533
was looking if they
had anything in common.

00:15:00.557 --> 00:15:02.146
And what jumped out on the resume

00:15:02.170 --> 00:15:04.234
was looking at extracurricular activities,

00:15:04.258 --> 00:15:07.186
things that were not necessarily
directly relevant to the job,

00:15:07.210 --> 00:15:09.641
and importantly,
they were very, very classed.

00:15:09.665 --> 00:15:12.189
AG: My read of your findings

00:15:12.213 --> 00:15:15.288
is that when interviewers
go in looking for culture fit,

00:15:15.312 --> 00:15:17.995
they often end up weeding out
diversity of background

00:15:18.019 --> 00:15:19.222
and diversity of thought.

00:15:19.968 --> 00:15:21.193
LR: Yes.

00:15:21.217 --> 00:15:22.827
AG: So that's scary.

00:15:22.851 --> 00:15:24.371
And that led me to say,

00:15:24.395 --> 00:15:26.847
"OK, well what can we do instead?"

00:15:26.871 --> 00:15:29.233
I'm sure you've come across
the great piece

00:15:29.257 --> 00:15:32.090
from Diego Rodriguez,
who used to be at IDEO,